An object-oriented program contains some upcasting somewhere, because that\rquote s how you decouple yourself from knowing about the exact type you\rquote re working with. Look at the code in }{\b doStuff(\~)}{:
\par }\pard\plain \s24\li360\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw15\brsp200 \adjustright \f6\fs20\lang1024\kerning18\cgrid {  s.erase();
