\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\adjustright \v\fs20\cgrid {\xe {function declaration syntax}}}{
A function declaration in C and C++ gives the function name, the argument types passed to the function, and the return value of the function. For example, here is a declaration for a function called }{\b func1(\~) }{that takes two integer arguments 
(integers are denoted in C/C++ with the keyword }{\b int}{) and returns an integer:
