), generated by the compiler, into an executable program the operating system can load and run. It is the last phase of the compilation process.
\par Linker characteristics vary from system to system. Generally, you just te
ll the linker the names of the object modules and libraries you want linked together, and the name of the executable, and it goes to work. Some systems require you to invoke the linker yourself. With most C++ packages you invoke the linker through the C++
