ave to worry that your particular library component is inside a namespace, since the }{\b using}{ directive makes that namespace available throughout the file where the }{\b using}{ directive was written.
\par Exposing all the elements from a namespace after someone has gone to the trouble to hide them may seem a bit counterproductive, and in fact you should be careful about thoughtlessly doing this (as you\rquote ll learn later in the book). However, the }{\b 
using}{ directive only exposes those names for the current file, so it is not quite so drastic as it first sounds (but think twice about doing it in a header file \endash  that }{\i is}{ reckless).
