 usually not an issue with modern compilers). For example, here\rquote s an extremely lazy declaration of the C function }{\b printf(\~) }{(from }{\b <stdio.h>}{):
\par }\pard\plain \s25\li360\sa60\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw15\brsp200 {\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \f6\fs20\lang1024\kerning18\cgrid {printf(...);
