functions have multiple representations for time, and these are all part of the }{\b Time}{ class. However, it isn\rquote t necessary to update all of them all the time, so instead the }{\b time_t T}{ is used as the base representation, and the }{\b 
tm local}{ and ASCII character representation }{\b asciiRep}{ each have flags to indicate if they\rquote ve been updated to the current }{\b time_t}{. The two }{\b private}{ functions }{\b updateLocal(\~)}{ and }{\b updateAscii(\~)}{
