 static data members}}}{\pard\plain \sa120\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \v\fs20\cgrid {\xe {static\: data members inside a class}}}{. There is a single piece of storage for a }{\b static}{
 data member, regardless of how many objects of that class you create. All objects share the same }{\b static}{ storage space for that data member, so it is a way for them to \ldblquote communicate\rdblquote  with each other. But the }{\b static}{
 data belongs to the class; its name is scoped inside the class and it can be }{\b public}{, }{\b private}{, or }{\b protected}{.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\li360\sb120\sa60\sl-480\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel2\adjustright \f4\fs44\lang1024\cgrid {{\*\bkmkstart _Toc312373949}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc451776168}De
fining storage for static data members{\*\bkmkend _Toc312373949}{\*\bkmkend _Toc451776168}
\par }\pard\plain \sa120\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {\pard\plain \sa120\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \v\fs20\cgrid {\xe {definition\: storage for static data members}}}
