\sa120\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \v\fs20\cgrid {\xe {member\: defining storage for static data member}}}{Because }{\b static}{
 data has a single piece of storage regardless of how many objects are created, that storage must be defined in a single place. The compiler will not allocate storage for you, although this was on
ce true, with some compilers. The linker will report an error if a }{\b static}{ data member is declared but not defined.
