{\pard\plain \sa120\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \v\fs20\cgrid {\xe {copy-constructor\: alternatives}}}{At this point your head may be
 swimming, and you might be wondering how you could have possibly written a functional class without knowing about the copy-constructor. But remember: You need a copy-constructor only if you\rquote re going to pass an object of your class }{\i by value}{
. If that never happens, you don\rquote t need a copy-constructor.
