\par It also turns out that many programmers seem to find C\rquote s dynamic memory functions too confusing and complicated; it\rquote s not uncommon to find C programmers who use virtual memory }{\pard\plain \sa120\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0
