) an object and then }{\b delete}{ it, the behavior is undefined. Because most default implementations of }{\b new}{ and }{\b delete}{ use }{\b malloc(\~)}{ and }{\b free(\~)}{, you\rquote ll probably release the memory without calling the destructor.

