 to use late binding. For efficiency\rquote s sake, most compilers will perform early binding}{\pard\plain \sa120\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \v\fs20\cgrid {\xe {early binding}}}{\pard\plain 
\sa120\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \v\fs20\cgrid {\xe {binding\: early binding}}}{ when they are making a call to a virtual function for an object because they know the exact type. Here\rquote s an example:
