\par The first chapter in this section introduces the Standard C++ }{\b string}{ class, which is a powerful tool that simplifies most of the text processing chores you might have to do. The }{\b string}{
 class may be the most thorough string manipulation tool you\rquote ve ever seen. Chances are, anything you\rquote ve done to character strings with lines of code in C can be done with a member function call in the string class, including }{\b append(\~)}
{, }{\b assign(\~)}{, }{\b insert(\~)}{, }{\b remove(\~)}{, }{\b replace(\~)}{, }{\b resize(\~)}{, }{\b copy(\~)}{, }{\b find(\~)}{, }{\b rfind(\~)}{, }{\b find_first_of(\~)}{, }{\b find_last_of(\~)}{, }{\b find_first_not_of(\~)}{, }{\b find_last_not_of(
\~)}{, }{\b substr(\~)}{, and }{\b compare(\~)}{. The operators }{\b =}{, }{\b +=}{, and }{\b [ ]}{ are also overloaded to perform the intuitive operations. In addition, there\rquote s a \ldblquote wide\rdblquote  }{\b wstring}{
 class designed to support international character sets. Both }{\b string}{ and }{\b wstring}{ (declared in }{\b <string>}{, not to be confused with C\rquote s }{\b <string.h>}{, which is, in strict C++, }{\b <cstring>}{
) are created from a common template class called }{\b basic_string}{. Note that the string classes are seamlessly integrated with iostreams}{\pard\plain \sa120\widctlpar\adjustright \v\fs20\cgrid {\xe {iostreams\: and Standard C++ library string class}}}
{, virtually eliminating the need for you to ever use }{\b strstream}{. 
\par The next chapter covers the }{\b iostream}{ library.
\par }{\b Language Support}{\pard\plain \sa120\widctlpar\adjustright \v\fs20\cgrid {\xe {Standard C++ libraries\: language support}}}{. Elements inherent to the language itself, like implementation limits}{\pard\plain \sa120\widctlpar\adjustright 
\v\fs20\cgrid {\xe {implementation\: limits}}}{\pard\plain \sa120\widctlpar\adjustright \v\fs20\cgrid {\xe {limits, implementation}}}{ in }{\b <climits>}{ and }{\b <cfloat>}{; dynamic memory declarations in }{\b <new>}{ like }{\b bad_alloc}{\pard\plain 
\sa120\widctlpar\adjustright \v\fs20\cgrid {\xe {bad_alloc}}}{ (the exception thrown when you\rquote re out of memory) and }{\b set_new_handler}{\pard\plain \sa120\widctlpar\adjustright \v\fs20\cgrid {\xe {set_new_handler}}}{; the }{\b <typeinfo>}{
 header for RTTI}{\pard\plain \sa120\widctlpar\adjustright \v\fs20\cgrid {\xe {run-time type identification}}}{ and the }{\b <exception>}{ header that declares the }{\b terminate(\~)}{\pard\plain \sa120\widctlpar\adjustright \v\fs20\cgrid {\xe {terminate(
\~)}}}{ and }{\b unexpected(\~)}{\pard\plain \sa120\widctlpar\adjustright \v\fs20\cgrid {\xe {unexpected(\~)}}}{ functions.
