\par }\pard\plain \sa120\widctlpar\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {The }{\b string}{ member function }{\b substr(\~)}{ takes a starting position as its first argument and the number of characters to select as the second argument. Bot
h of these arguments have default values and if you say }{\b substr(\~)}{ with an empty argument list you produce a copy of the entire }{\b string}{, so this is a convenient way to duplicate a }{\b string}{. 
\par Here\rquote s what the }{\b string}{ }{\b quoteMe }{contains after the initialization shown above :
