\par The default constructor sets the private }{\b FILE}{ pointer }{\b f}{ to zero. But now, before any reference to }{\b f}{, its value must be checked to ensure it isn\rquote t zero. This is accomplished with the last member function in the class, }{\b F(\~)
}{, which is }{\b private}{ because it is intended to be used only by other member functions. (We don\rquote t want to give the user direct access to the }{\b FILE}{ structure in this class.)}{\cs23\fs16\up6 \chftn {\footnote \pard\plain 
