 Standard C++ library string class}}}{\pard\plain \sa120\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \v\fs20\cgrid {\xe {class\: Standard C++ string}}}{. All these stream objects have the same interface, regardless of whether you
\rquote re working with a file, standard I/O, a piece of memory or a }{\b string}{ object. The single interface you learn also works for extensions added to support new classes.
\par If a stream is capable of producing bytes (an istream), you can get information from the stream using an extractor. The extractor produces and formats the type of information that\rquote 
