{\pard\plain \sa120\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \v\fs20\cgrid {\xe {temporary\: object}}}{is created by the call to the }{\b Fixw}{ constructor, and that temporary is passed to }{\b operator<<}{
. The effect is that of a manipulator with arguments.
\par The }{\b Bin}{ effector relies on the fact that shifting an unsigned number to the right shifts zeros into the high bits. ULONG_MAX }{\pard\plain \sa120\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \v\fs20\cgrid {\xe {ULONG_MAX}}}{
(the largest }{\b unsigned long}{ value, from the standard include file }{\b <climits>}{ }{\pard\plain \sa120\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \v\fs20\cgrid {\xe {LIMITS.H}}}{
) is used to produce a value with the high bit set, and this value is moved across the number in question (by shifting it), masking each bit.
\par Initially the problem with this technique was that once you created a class called }{\b Fixw}{ for }{\b char*}{ or }{\b Bin }{for }{\b unsigned long}{,}{\b  }{no one else could create a different }{\b Fixw}{ or }{\b Bin }{
class for their type. However, with }{\i namespaces}{ }{\pard\plain \sa120\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \v\fs20\cgrid {\xe {namespace}}}{(covered in Chapter XX), this problem is eliminated.
