pects. The second argument is the number of bytes to write, which is the size of the }{\b DataPoint}{ object. Because no pointers are contained in }{\b DataPoint}{
, there is no problem in writing the object to disk. If the object is more sophisticated, you must implement a scheme for }{\i serialization}{ }{\pard\plain \sa120\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \v\fs20\cgrid {\xe {
