StringVector.cpp}{ and package it into a class for later reuse.
\par Now the question is: do you create a member object of type }{\b vector}{, or do you inherit? A general guideline is t
o always prefer composition (member objects) over inheritance, but with the STL this is often not true, because there are so many existing algorithms that work with the STL types that you may want your new type to }{\i be}{ an STL type. So the list of }{
\b string}{s}{\b  }{should also }{\i be}{ a }{\b vector}{, thus inheritance is desired.
\par }\pard\plain \s24\li360\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw15\brsp200 \adjustright \f6\fs20\lang1024\kerning18\cgrid {//: C20:FileEditor.h
