}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc451776477}Exception matching{\*\bkmkend _Toc305593301}{\*\bkmkend _Toc305628773}{\*\bkmkend _Toc312374124}{\*\bkmkend _Toc451776477}
\par }\pard\plain \sa120\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {\pard\plain \sa120\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \v\fs20\cgrid {\xe {exception handling\: exception matching}}}{
When an exception is thrown, the exception-handling system looks through the \ldblquote nearest\rdblquote  handlers in the order they are written. When it finds a match, the exception is considered handled, and no further searching occurs. 
\par Matching an exception doesn\rquote t require a perfect match between the exception and its handler. An object or refer
