gram that handles POSTs. The only thing you need to do is get the data from a }{\b Post }{object instead of from the }{\b QUERY_STRING}{ environment variable. The following listing shows how simple it is to write such a CGI program:
\par }\pard\plain \s24\li360\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\brdrl\brdrs\brdrw15\brsp200 {\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \f6\fs20\lang1024\kerning18\cgrid {//: C26:CGI_POST.cpp
